      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty stark way to frame it. You mentioned the \"existential threat\" of climate change, but some analysts argue that the transition is being rushed too quickly, creating real risks for low-income households due to skyrocketing utility bills. Can you go into more detail on the arguments from the side concerned about these economic impacts? I want to make sure I'm not missing the nuances of their position.",
